1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:03,450
So we've discussed that
tracking monitors

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,685
the progress of
project activities.

3
00:00:05,685 --> 00:00:07,395
But you may still be wondering,

4
00:00:07,395 --> 00:00:09,735
what specifically
should you be tracking?

5
00:00:09,735 --> 00:00:11,760
I'll take you through a few of

6
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,770
the most commonly
tracked items that I

7
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:16,545
found helpful when managing
projects at Google.

8
00:00:16,545 --> 00:00:19,965
First, you should always
track the project schedule.

9
00:00:19,965 --> 00:00:22,970
This is made up of tasks
and activities that ensure

10
00:00:22,970 --> 00:00:24,350
that the project is effectively

11
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:25,870
heading toward its
completion date.

12
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:27,860
After all, your
ultimate goal is to

13
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,340
complete your
deliverables on time.

14
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:33,515
Equally important is tracking
the status of action items,

15
00:00:33,515 --> 00:00:35,690
key tasks, and
activities to ensure

16
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:38,045
that that work is
actually getting done.

17
00:00:38,045 --> 00:00:40,070
Tracking tasks also helps to

18
00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:42,745
track your team's progress
toward milestones.

19
00:00:42,745 --> 00:00:44,810
We learned a bit
more about tracking

20
00:00:44,810 --> 00:00:47,555
progress toward milestones
earlier in the course,

21
00:00:47,555 --> 00:00:50,060
and we stressed the
importance of creating tasks

22
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:52,720
and milestones to keep
everyone on track.

23
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,765
When you're in the
middle of a project,

24
00:00:54,765 --> 00:00:57,135
new tasks will come
up all the time.

25
00:00:57,135 --> 00:00:59,195
In order to avoid
missing deadlines,

26
00:00:59,195 --> 00:01:01,370
it's imperative to
track tasks as they

27
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:04,120
progress and as you
approach key milestones.

28
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:07,520
Next, you'll also need to
track costs to ensure that

29
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:10,900
you don't overspend or
underspend on project tasks.

30
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:12,320
As I mentioned earlier,

31
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:13,790
all projects have budgets,

32
00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:16,325
and whether or not you're
overseeing the entire budget,

33
00:01:16,325 --> 00:01:18,170
you may be overseeing tasks and

34
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:20,740
resources that have
budget implications.

35
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:24,215
Finally, you'll need to track
key decisions, changes,

36
00:01:24,215 --> 00:01:26,690
dependencies, and
risks to the project,

37
00:01:26,690 --> 00:01:29,165
including any agreed
upon scope changes.

38
00:01:29,165 --> 00:01:31,640
This way, your team and
stakeholders are aligned

39
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:34,280
on what needs to be done
for the project to succeed.

40
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:36,440
We will cover this in
more detail throughout

41
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:39,340
the course since it's a big
part of running the project.

42
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:42,320
To recap, the items that are
helpful to track throughout

43
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:45,710
the project execution phase
include the project schedule,

44
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:48,304
which contains the key
tasks and activities,

45
00:01:48,304 --> 00:01:50,180
the status of action items,

46
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,900
progress toward milestones, costs,

47
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,960
and key decisions and changes.

48
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,810
There are many moving parts to be

49
00:01:56,810 --> 00:01:58,805
aware of once a
project is underway.

50
00:01:58,805 --> 00:02:01,220
Tracking them closely
benefits you and

51
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:03,805
your team as you head
toward the project goal.

52
00:02:03,805 --> 00:02:05,750
I've taken you through
an introduction

53
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:07,265
to tracking, and coming up,

54
00:02:07,265 --> 00:02:09,380
we'll discuss project
management tools and

55
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:12,200
templates you can use to
track project activities.

56
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:16,050
Meet me in the next video
to expand your toolkit.
